codex
The first proof exposed a backend simplification gap, not a source-semantic gap: after indexing, the fixed method rule constructs a one-character sequence, but the prover does not reduce the constructor-disjoint equality `iCons(...) ==K .IntSeq`. I’m adding the narrow derived constructor-disjointness lemma that the residual identifies. It neither computes the function’s answer nor bypasses execution; it only states that a nonempty constructor is not the empty constructor.
apply patch
patch: completed
